statement:
Let X be a separable metric space with its Borel σ-algebra. There is a family P : ℕ → ℕ → Set X such that:
(1) every P i j is Borel;
(2) for each i, the sets P i j (j ∈ ℕ) are pairwise disjoint;
(3) for each i, ∪_j P i j = X;
(4) for all i, j, any two points x, x′ ∈ P i j satisfy dist(x, x′) < 1/(i+1);
(5) for all i, j there is k with P (i+1) j ⊆ P i k, i.e. each partition refines the previous one.
